        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0567" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.01/10–2144: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-30T16:00:00-04:00">October 30, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–585. The Department would like to receive from the Embassy such information as
                    may be available concerning the present Spanish attitude toward Spain’s future
                    position in Tangier. In this connection <pb facs="0568" n="556" xml:id="pg556"/>
                    reference is made to telegrams no. 312 of October 19 and 313 of October 21 from
                    the Legation at Tangier. Since the latter telegram appears not to have been
                    repeated to Madrid the Embassy will doubtless wish to ask Tangier for the text.
                    Is it the opinion of the Embassy that the withdrawal of Spanish regiments has
                    any association with this question, as suggested by the Legation?</p>
                <p>Copy to Tangier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
